messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI systems become deeply integrated into work, education, and software.",
      "detail": "Productivity rises with uneven gains; debates over safety, labor, and misinformation intensify. Climate adaptation spending accelerates after severe weather seasons."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global CO2 emissions peak and begin a sustained decline.",
      "detail": "EVs dominate new vehicle sales and coal power nears phase-out in many regions. Some countries lag, keeping the transition uneven."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "General-purpose AI automates a majority of cognitive tasks across industries.",
      "detail": "Output surges and many professions restructure while new sectors emerge. Governments expand social safety nets and large-scale reskilling."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "Gene and cell therapies become routine for dozens of conditions.",
      "detail": "Cancer survival improves markedly and rare-disease burdens drop. Ethical and access debates persist."
    },
    {
      "year": 2039,
      "event": "A major AI failure or misuse triggers global safety and audit treaties.",
      "detail": "After a high-profile incident, mandatory evaluations, incident reporting, and compute oversight become standard. International coordination reduces but does not eliminate systemic risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Climate impacts intensify with more severe heatwaves, floods, and crop stresses.",
      "detail": "Adaptation infrastructure and climate-resilient agriculture scale. Insurance and finance reprice risk globally."
    },
    {
      "year": 2043,
      "event": "Grid-scale storage prices collapse, enabling very high renewable penetration.",
      "detail": "Firm power is supplied through a mix of storage, nuclear, geothermal, and enhanced transmission. Blackout risks fall as grid orchestration improves."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First commercial fusion pilot plant delivers net electricity to the grid.",
      "detail": "It proves technical viability but remains expensive; learning curves begin. Hybrid clean grids accelerate fossil decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Large blocs achieve net-zero and global emissions fall sharply.",
      "detail": "Carbon removal scales to balance hard-to-abate sectors. Air quality and health outcomes improve."
    },
    {
      "year": 2053,
      "event": "Managed retreat from high-risk coasts and river deltas becomes widespread.",
      "detail": "New inland cities and protective works expand. Cultural heritage preservation and equitable relocation dominate policy debates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "AI governance matures with enforceable global standards and liability regimes.",
      "detail": "Autonomous systems gain constrained legal agency for contracts and accountability. Many governments require licensing for frontier training runs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "World population peaks then begins a gradual decline.",
      "detail": "Aging societies pivot to automation and immigration. Productivity relies heavily on AI and robotics."
    },
    {
      "year": 2063,
      "event": "First crewed Mars mission lands while lunar industry scales rapidly.",
      "detail": "The Mars mission is exploratory and dependent on Earth. The Moon supplies propellant and metals for cis-lunar infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "Carefully governed solar radiation modification field trials occur.",
      "detail": "Small, temporary interventions validate models and monitoring. Society keeps SRM as a limited backstop, not a substitute for mitigation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Longevity therapies extend healthy lifespan toward 100–120 years for many.",
      "detail": "Retirement and life-course norms shift. Healthspan gains exceed lifespan gains, keeping frailty later."
    },
    {
      "year": 2082,
      "event": "A small, continuously occupied Mars settlement is established.",
      "detail": "It relies on closed-loop life support with periodic resupply. Science, prestige, and commercial niches justify costs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Global mean sea level exceeds 0.6 meters above 2000 baseline.",
      "detail": "Coastal defenses and relocations continue for decades. Some low-lying nations complete relocations with diaspora support."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming stabilizes near ~2°C with ongoing adaptation and restoration.",
      "detail": "Many ecosystems are transformed; targeted rewilding and assisted migration help partial recovery. Food and water systems are more resilient but still climate-sensitive."
    },
    {
      "year": 2110,
      "event": "First beamed-sail interstellar probe launched toward Alpha Centauri.",
      "detail": "Data return is expected late in the millennium. Laser infrastructure doubles as space-industry backbone."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Fusion and advanced fission provide abundant, cheap, dispatchable power worldwide.",
      "detail": "Energy abundance unlocks desalination, materials recycling, and synthetic fuels at scale. Energy geopolitics softens, though critical minerals remain strategic."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "High-bandwidth neural interfaces and cognitive augmentation are commonplace.",
      "detail": "Education and creativity accelerate; privacy and autonomy protections expand. Cultural norms differentiate 'baseline' and 'augmented' communities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2175,
      "event": "Hybrid human–AI polities co-govern major regions and platforms.",
      "detail": "Constitutional AI and oversight institutions are entrenched. Work focuses on design, care, research, and stewardship."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Biodiversity sees net gains in many regions under active restoration.",
      "detail": "Extinctions leave permanent gaps, but functional ecosystems recover. Large wildlife corridors and marine reserves span continents and oceans."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Lunar and Martian economies integrate with Earth via regular logistics and data links.",
      "detail": "Space industry supplies materials, propellants, and computing from low-gravity sites. Governance balances local autonomy with shared law."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level is 1–2 meters above 2000, with centuries of managed adaptation normalized.",
      "detail": "Floating districts, surge barriers, and retreat have reshaped coasts. Cultural centers persist but many sites are memorialized rather than inhabited."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Orbital industry and habitats expand dramatically around Earth and the inner solar system.",
      "detail": "Solar power satellites and asteroid mining are routine. Millions live in free-space habitats with diverse cultures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Human lineages diversify into baseline, bioengineered, and largely digital minds.",
      "detail": "Interoperability standards and rights frameworks maintain broad cohesion. The concept of 'humanity' becomes inclusive and plural."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Autonomous interstellar precursors establish resource nodes in nearby systems.",
      "detail": "Crewed or embodied travel remains slow, but network effects begin bridging light-years. Governance treaties manage replication and biosphere protection."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Civilizational continuity persists through robust knowledge preservation and institutions.",
      "detail": "Languages and cultures have diversified widely. Long-term climate management is bureaucratized and routine."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Ice sheet responses approach new equilibria; sea level stabilizes several meters above 2000.",
      "detail": "Coastal geographies are permanently altered. Inland megaregions flourish around climate-stable zones."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Carbon cycle rebalances close to preindustrial ranges with active management.",
      "detail": "Earth system stewardship becomes a conservative, values-driven enterprise. Archaeological layers of the Anthropocene are carefully curated."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "A resilient, multi-planetary civilization is the norm, with mature planetary defense.",
      "detail": "Asteroid and comet threats are routinely deflected. Energy and materials circularity are near-complete."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Large-scale terraforming and climate control on Mars and in habitats reach late stages.",
      "detail": "Mars supports open-air activity in limited regions. Free-space ecologies are sophisticated and self-maintaining."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Biological and digital descendants maintain deep interoperability across substrates.",
      "detail": "Some biosapient groups speciate, while cultural identity anchors shared 'human' affiliation. Rights regimes adapt to diverse forms."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Interstellar settlements and relay networks span dozens of light-years.",
      "detail": "Travel and communication remain limited by light speed, but cultural exchange persists. Local autonomy is high, with weak but enduring federations."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Extensive solar system engineering creates a partial Dyson-swarm–like infrastructure.",
      "detail": "Solar energy capture rises by orders of magnitude. Environmental protections keep Earth’s biosphere largely intact."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Plural, spacefaring civilizations—biological and digital—persist with continuity to early human cultures.",
      "detail": "Earth is a protected cradle and living museum amid thriving off-world societies. Future trajectories remain open, with major risks managed but never eliminated."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "The most likely path is survival through turbulent 21st–22nd centuries marked by climate stress and AI disruption, followed by consolidation into an abundant, multi-planetary, and increasingly plural civilization. Risks from AI, bio, and conflict cause shocks but also drive governance and resilience, making outright extinction unlikely yet not impossible. Over millennia, definitions of humanity blur as biological, enhanced, and digital descendants coexist."
}
